<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waterford</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vedrarfjord</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waterford is a city and port in south-eastern Ireland on the estuary of the River Suir. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> in 914, it is the oldest city in Ireland and was a Norse trading town until Anglo-Norman forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a> captured it in 1170. Henry II landed there in 1171, and it became a royal city of the Lordship of Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waterford.jpg" alt="Waterford" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nmwalsh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reginalds_Tower_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Ptolemy's Geography of about 150 lists the Brigantes in south-eastern Ireland, usually placed in the area of modern Wexford and <b>Waterford</b>, near the Coriondi and the Usdiae.</blockquote><a href="/state/brigantes-ireland">Brigantes (Ireland)</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Anglo-Normans took <b>Waterford</b> in 1170 their lands were granted to settlers, and the kingdom faded around 1200.</blockquote><a href="/state/deisi-muman">Deisi Muman</a></li><li><blockquote>Anglo-Norman knights led by Strongbow, who married Diarmait's daughter Aoife, took Wexford, <b>Waterford</b> and Dublin.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Kingdom of Leinster</a></li><li><blockquote>Vikings raided the south-east in the 9th century, and in 914 a large fleet under Ragnall established a base at <b>Waterford</b>, Vedrafjordr.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-waterford">Kingdom of Waterford</a></li><li><blockquote>Henry II landed at <b>Waterford</b> in 1171 to control Strongbow and other Norman adventurers.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-ireland">Lordship of Ireland</a></li></ul></section>
